# Go, SQL, and TypeScript are LF everywhere. Without this, a Windows checkout
# materializes CRLF working-tree files that gofmt -l flags on every run, which
# makes the "gofmt must print nothing" gate unverifiable.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
# A .1pux is a ZIP archive, and the import fixture is a real one. Without this,
# `text=auto` has to guess, and a guess of "text" would rewrite bytes inside the
# archive and break both its CRCs and the ZIP magic detection keys on.
*.1pux binary
